    "https://www.georgefox.edu/offices/hr/careers/index.html": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Jobs at George Fox University | Christian College in Oregon Skip to main content Skip to footer Academics Admissions About Athletics Giving Request Info Apply Search George Fox Careers at George Fox Benefits & Perks Tuition Remission Careers at George Fox At George Fox University, we believe we do more than come to work. Every day, in every encounter, we’re answering a call to serve our students, coworkers, alumni and university supporters. Faculty Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Non-Faculty Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Adjunct Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Where Your Personal Purpose and Career Align We’re passionate about the work we do. Whether you’re in the front of a classroom, coaching athletes on the field, or stewarding our funds behind the scenes, all of our work serves the same mission: to educate and inspire students to pursue God’s calling . Explore Who We Are What Drives Us: Mission, Vision, and Values What Shapes Us: Statement of Faith How We Live: Community Lifestyle Statement Our Commitment to Diversity watch video A Great Place to Work Close Best Christian Workplaces Certified George Fox University has been recognized as a Certified Best Christian Workplace for 2026, becoming one of just 10 higher education institutions nationally in the last two years to receive that designation. The recognition honors organizations that demonstrate intentional leadership and a commitment to cultivating a healthy, flourishing workplace culture marked by high employee engagement . The accomplishment is underscored by the fact o nly 34% of participating higher education institutions achieve certification. Certified organizations score at least 4.0 out of 5.0 on the Best Christian Workplaces Employee Engagement Survey, reflecting strong organizational culture. This distinction affirms our commitment to fostering a supportive, mission-driven environment where employees feel valued, engaged and empowered in their work. Tamara Wytsma Director of Outreach, Engagement and Innovation: Division of Engineering, Science, Art, & Business Each day, I have the opportunity to touch the life of a college student in some small way. Fox is my place of employment, but it is also where God has placed me to serve. Twenty years from now, I believe I will look back on this season and say that these were some of the most fulfilling and fun years of my life!\" Benefits and Perks We proudly offer our employees a comprehensive benefits package and a suite of perks to enrich your life as you contribute to our community and mission. Our employees enjoy: A 403(b) retirement plan with 6% employer-paid contributions Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, prescription and alternative care coverage A tuition remission program for employees, their spouses and/or dependent children 17 paid holidays per year Generous paid time off (PTO), sick and parental leave Free access for employees and membership options for their immediate family to our fitness and recreation facility, the Hadlock Student Center Access to the nearby Chehalem Aquatic Center Remote and hybrid work options for some positions Spiritual and professional development opportunities Numerous volunteer opportunities Learn more about our employee benefits and perks Let Us Pay for You and Your Family’s Education Learn about the tuition remission benefit for you as an employee, your spouse, and your dependents, as well as our tuition exchange program. A Place to Thrive Our love of students drives our work, but our community is what makes us unique. At George Fox, you’ll find that you’re not just coming to work; you’re joining a community of professionals who care about your aspirations and your spiritual growth. Diversity & Inclusion We believe a diverse community is a reflection of God’s kingdom, so we strive to create an inclusive atmosphere and prioritize diversity in our programming, hiring and recruiting practices. Read more about diversity at George Fox Faith Integration Here, employees are Christ-followers who align with our mission, vision and values . They are invited to join our weekly chapel services, lead small groups of students in studying God’s Word, pray for one another, participate in our annual Day of Prayer, and serve God and others, including at our annual Serve Day . Read the story of how one professor answered God’s nudge and baptized three students during class Work-Life Balance We care about your life outside of work, which is why we prioritize work-life balance. George Fox provides generous paid time off and 17 annual holidays, and we allow flexibility in your schedule and working location. Joy-Filled Community We’re a community that values the unique contributions each person brings. It isn’t unusual for coworkers to pray for one another and assist each other in tangible ways – or for departments to collectively celebrate a job well done. watch video A Diverse Community Close watch video Work-Life Balance Close watch video What Serve Day Means for Our Community Close What People Love About Working at George Fox I'm thankful to be part of a God-seeking, God-honoring community, especially with my closest colleagues. Helen Morse Administrative Assistant, George Fox Honors Program [Getting the opportunity to] attend chapel means not tending to something else (like my inbox)! I’m grateful for a mini-sabbath during the week – a recognition that we are more than what we do or produce. Rick Muthiah Director of Learning Support Services Fox is a place I have always wanted to teach at. I’ve taught in the secular world for several years, but you can’t talk about your faith there. [Here at George Fox], I can incorporate my curriculum with Christianity and talk about God and the Bible with my students. Jessica Lopresti Professor of Communications I love the community at George Fox. I love the people I get to work with and the fact that we all have a common goal of serving students. I also love that we’re constantly looking for ways to grow, improve and change, and it’s never stagnant. It’s a part of our culture here to focus on becoming better people and learning to serve students better. Rachel Ryan Assistant Registrar Come Work With Us Working at George Fox is equal parts career and calling – a special community where students are put first, Christ is at the center of everything we do, and innovation drives us. We’re always looking for missionally minded candidates who are passionate about using their intellect, heart and faith in God to help impact and equip the next generation. We are looking for people who are: Faithful to God Thoughtful Mission-focused Driven and innovative Collaborative Humble Adaptable Check Out Our Current Opportunities Faculty Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Non-Faculty Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Adjunct Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Questions? Contact our Office of People & Culture: Phone: 503-554-2180 Email: georgefoxcareers@georgefox.edu Faculty Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Non-Faculty Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates Adjunct Jobs External Candidates Internal Candidates George Fox University: Newberg Campus 414 N. Meridian St Newberg,\n                OR\n                97132 503-538-8383 Information For Prospective Students Current Students Parents & Families of Current Students Alumni Current Employees Current Faculty Community Members Resources A-Z Index Blog Calendar Contact Us Find an Employee Jobs at George Fox Locations Quick Links MyGeorgeFox Canvas Email Search George Fox Be Known © 2026, George Fox University. All rights reserved. Privacy Consumer Information Non-Discrimination Policy Title IX / Sexual Misconduct Reporting"
    }
